temporal 11	# the temporal relations (between, meets, overlaps, during, equals) are offered at every file that has a start (source_attributes, SEN:sourceAttributes), not only at events (11; 10: more event types: holidays and observances (10; 9: Event has the icon Calendar by Matthew McClintock (DSL), the Calendar keeps the one by zuMi (9; 8: the items of the Events relation of a calendar are materialised as events (materialise_as, SEN:materialiseAs: Copy to Library, relations of an item) (8; 7: the events of a calendar are a self relation (like the outline of a document) and the relations of an event are in the group Temporal (7; 6: a calendar file (text/calendar, which Haiku gives no icon) has the calendar icon in the MIME database of the user (6; 5: the Calendar (the umbrella of the events of a calendar file, relation Events), the relation Description (the Markdown file of the description) and the event has the fields of a calendar file (uid, location, organizer, status, attendance, url, meeting URL and type, recurrence) and the relations Attendee, Takes place at and Series (5; 4: the event type has its values in the MIME type (SEN:ATTR:VALUES) for the list that follows the field; 3: Description is viewable; 2: Between, the event types, the Calendar icon by zuMi, the folder of the relations; 1: the first version))
